# Service credits — Acme Cloud Systems / Northwind Logistics (ACME-NW-MSA-2026)

> Module Service_credit_acme_northwind

Sources: SYN-002 (Exhibit A, standard SLA, 2026-01-01) and SYN-003 § 4.2 (Order Form No. 1,
effective 2026-07-01). `monthly_uptime` is a percentage expressed as a plain decimal
(99.5 means 99.5%); `month` is the first day of the affected calendar month.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ServiceCredit:
  input service_month content date
  input monthly_uptime content decimal
  input monthly_service_fee content money
  input request_date content date

  internal order_form_applies condition
  internal credit_deadline content date

  output eligible content boolean
  output credit_percentage content decimal
  output credit content money
```

## SYN-003 — the Order Form's tier table governs months from its effective date

  Order Form effective date: July 1, 2026. […] The Service Credit table in Section A.3 of
  Exhibit A to the MSA is replaced, for the Services ordered under this Order Form, with
  the following […]

Authority for treating this as an exception rather than a competing definition:
SYN-001 § 14.3 (Order of Precedence) and SYN-003 § 6.1.

```catala
scope ServiceCredit:
  rule order_form_applies under condition service_month >= |2026-07-01|
  consequence fulfilled
```

## SYN-002 § A.4.1 — the claim window

  To receive a Service Credit, Customer must submit a request to Acme support within
  thirty (30) days after the end of the calendar month in which the Downtime occurred.
  Requests submitted after that period are not eligible.

```catala
scope ServiceCredit:
  definition credit_deadline equals (service_month + 1 month) + 30 day
  definition eligible equals request_date <= credit_deadline
```

## SYN-002 § A.2–A.3 — the standard commitment and tier table

  Acme will make the Services available with a Monthly Uptime Percentage of at least
  99.9% during each calendar month. […] Less than 99.9% but equal to or greater than
  99.0% → 10%; less than 99.0% but equal to or greater than 95.0% → 25%; less than
  95.0% → 100%.

```catala
scope ServiceCredit:
  label commitment_met
  definition credit_percentage equals 0%

  label std_tier_1 exception commitment_met
  definition credit_percentage
    under condition
      not order_form_applies
      and monthly_uptime < 99.9 and monthly_uptime >= 99.0
    consequence equals 10%

  label std_tier_2 exception commitment_met
  definition credit_percentage
    under condition
      not order_form_applies
      and monthly_uptime < 99.0 and monthly_uptime >= 95.0
    consequence equals 25%

  label std_tier_3 exception commitment_met
  definition credit_percentage
    under condition not order_form_applies and monthly_uptime < 95.0
    consequence equals 100%
```

## SYN-003 § 4.2 — the Enterprise tier table

  Less than 99.9% but equal to or greater than 99.0% → 15%; less than 99.0% but equal to
  or greater than 95.0% → 30%; less than 95.0% → 100%.

```catala
scope ServiceCredit:
  label ent_tier_1 exception commitment_met
  definition credit_percentage
    under condition
      order_form_applies
      and monthly_uptime < 99.9 and monthly_uptime >= 99.0
    consequence equals 15%

  label ent_tier_2 exception commitment_met
  definition credit_percentage
    under condition
      order_form_applies
      and monthly_uptime < 99.0 and monthly_uptime >= 95.0
    consequence equals 30%

  label ent_tier_3 exception commitment_met
  definition credit_percentage
    under condition order_form_applies and monthly_uptime < 95.0
    consequence equals 100%
```

## SYN-002 § A.4.2 — the monthly ceiling, and the credit itself

  Service Credits in any calendar month shall not exceed one hundred percent (100%) of
  the Monthly Service Fee for the affected Service.

The tier tables top out at 100%, so the ceiling binds only if a future document raises a
tier above it; it is encoded because the clause says so, not because a tier needs it.

```catala
scope ServiceCredit:
  definition credit equals
    if not eligible then $0
    else if credit_percentage > 100% then monthly_service_fee
    else monthly_service_fee * credit_percentage
```
